  "rule": [
    "Read the entry's param_constraints member (absent or null means none). A field's constraint counts only when it is an object whose allowed member is a non-empty list; a missing or non-list order is an empty order. A malformed constraint counts as no constraint.",
    "If the request does not carry the field at its wire path for the format, change nothing: never add a field.",
    "With a constraint for the field: an accepted value (in allowed) is kept. A value in order but not accepted becomes the accepted value nearest to it by position in order; on a tie the higher value wins. Accepted values that are not in order are never picked as nearest. A value not in order, or with no accepted value in order, is kept as sent.",
    "With no constraint for the field: Go's mappings apply. chat_completions reasoning_effort \"xhigh\" becomes \"high\"; messages output_config.effort \"xhigh\" becomes \"max\". Exact case, JSON strings only. Any other value is kept.",
    "Values compare as JSON values."
  ],
  "how_to_run": "For each case, parse param_constraints (a case with no param_constraints key is an entry without the member), then normalize value for field and format. expect is the value to send. A case with no value key is a request that does not carry the field: the rewritten request must not carry it either.",
